# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# A section's line is made longer or shorter in the plan: with the section
# selected (its properties shown, nothing else selected), a press on an
# end of its line drags that end along the line, so the section keeps its
# direction; the line stays at least half a metre long, the section shown
# follows, and the drag is one undo step.
import ui/editor/bim_editor.dl

function check section resize {boolean:passed} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if passed = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

function the section resize line of {a 64 bit integer:viewId} in {bim editor record:editor}:
    execute:
        set found to the bim view index of viewId in editor's documentValue's current
        set viewValue to the item at found's position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)
        return ((((the string form of "(") + (the string form of viewValue's lineStart's x)) + ((the string form of ", ") + (the string form of viewValue's lineStart's y))) + ((the string form of ") to (") + (the string form of viewValue's lineFinish's x))) + (((the string form of ", ") + (the string form of viewValue's lineFinish's y)) + (the string form of ")"))

# Moves the pointer to (x, y) as the plan does, without a snap target near.
function drag section resize pointer to {a 64 bit floating-point number:x} and {a 64 bit floating-point number:y} in {a pointer to a bim editor record:editor}:
    execute:
        move bim editor pointer to (a cad vector2 with x x and y y) within 0.08 in editor

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
set sectionId to add bim section view from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 2.0) to target
show bim editor section view sectionId in e
set editor's propertiesViewId to sectionId
select bim editor bim nothing picked numbered (the bim refused id) in e
set editor's propertiesViewId to sectionId
check section resize ((the bim selected section of editor) = sectionId) named (the string form of "the section is selected")

# Its finish dragged out to (9, 2.4): the line grows along itself to 9 m.
drag section resize pointer to 6.0 and 2.0 in e
press bim editor pointer in e
check section resize (editor's sectionDragId = sectionId) named (the string form of "a press on the line's finish takes its end")
drag section resize pointer to 7.5 and 2.2 in e
drag section resize pointer to 9.0 and 2.4 in e
release bim editor pointer in e
print (the section resize line of sectionId in editor) as a line
print editor's message as a line
set found to the bim view index of sectionId in editor's documentValue's current
set grown to the item at found's position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)
check section resize (((the absolute value of (grown's lineFinish's x - 9.0)) < 0.06) and ((the absolute value of (grown's lineFinish's y - 2.0)) < 1e-9)) named (the string form of "the finish moves along the line, not across")
check section resize (((the absolute value of (editor's sectionSecond's x - grown's lineFinish's x)) < 1e-9) and (editor's sectionDragId = the bim refused id)) named (the string form of "the section shown follows")

# Its start dragged past the finish: the line keeps half a metre.
set editor's propertiesViewId to sectionId
drag section resize pointer to 0.0 and 2.0 in e
press bim editor pointer in e
drag section resize pointer to 4.0 and 2.0 in e
drag section resize pointer to 12.0 and 2.0 in e
release bim editor pointer in e
print (the section resize line of sectionId in editor) as a line
set found to the bim view index of sectionId in editor's documentValue's current
set shortened to the item at found's position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)
check section resize ((the absolute value of ((the cad distance from shortened's lineStart to shortened's lineFinish) - 0.5)) < 1e-6) named (the string form of "the line stays at least half a metre long")

# One undo step brings the shortening back.
ignore undo bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
print (the section resize line of sectionId in editor) as a line
set found to the bim view index of sectionId in editor's documentValue's current
set undone to the item at found's position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)
check section resize ((the absolute value of (undone's lineStart's x - 0.0)) < 0.06) named (the string form of "undo restores the start")

# With an element selected, a press at the line's end does not drag it.
set editor's propertiesViewId to sectionId
set editor's selectionKind to bim wall picked
check section resize ((the bim selected section of editor) = the bim refused id) named (the string form of "no section handles while an element is selected")
